Helicopter Rotor Hub degrees of freedom
oFlapping hinges: Allows blade to
flap up or down. Avoids
transmission of bending moments
to the shaft
oLead-Lag hinges: Avoids stresses
at the blade root due to Coriolis
forces.
(Lead-lag motion neglected from
aerodynamic perspective)
oPitch / Feathering (bearing, swash
plate, pitch links): Control blade
pitch for controlling helicopter
motion.


Hub type: Rigid
oOnly feathering (pitching), No Flapping
oMoments transmitted to the rotor head
oHigh degree of control power.
oFewer parts ➔ less maintenance
http://www.helistart.com/RotorheadTypes.aspx


Hub type: Teetering
oBlades connected together through a common pivot
oBlades fixed at an average coning angle to reduce stress
oRotor disc can tilt in any direction
oLesser degree of control compared to rigid system
http://www.helistart.com/RotorheadTypes.aspx


